  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 950 PM MDT Thu Oct 29 2026\n\nTropical moisture continues over much of the CWA this evening (00Z \nKEPZ sounding still has 1.01 inches of PW). Expect a few showers \nand thunderstorms to continue overnight. Hi-res models have been \nvery inconsistent, but latest HRRR/FV3 show one last batch of \nrain/storms from about the Cont Divide east and drifting east, \nmostly done by around 12Z-14Z...perhaps driven by a short wave \njust south of the NM Bootheel. \n\nOur next weather system is currently organizing just west of the \nBaja as a strong sub-tropical jet pushes moisture into the area \nFriday. GFS/ECMWF have been pretty consistent, moving the upper \ntrough to eastern Arizona Friday afternoon. This will begin \nspreading showers/thunderstorms to the western CWA, with the rain \nspreading east over most of the remainder of the CWA by around \nmidnight. PWs still hang around one inch so flooding will still be a \nthreat for the last half of Friday. Mid-level winds do pick up as \nthe upper jet approaches so storms should move faster. Daytime CAPES \nof up to 500 J/kg along with some shear suggest some strong/severe \nstorms possible. Models showing rain should be done late Saturday \nmorning/mid-day, just in time for a dry trick-or-treat evening.\n\nFinally, the main upper trough and frontal system will sweep in \nSunday. Once again, showers/thunderstorms will develop west of \nDeming in the afternoon and rapidly spread east by late \nevening/early Monday morning. This may be more typical Fall, low \nenergy, fast moving type showers as very little instability develops \nand strong mid-level winds should speed the showers through. Surface \ncold front sweeps through El Paso early evening and showers should \nend shortly after fropa. A few showers could linger far east to \naround noon Monday. Warm temperatures of Sunday will fall back below \nnormal Monday and Tuesday. The good news is a drying trend is in \nstore through Thursday, before another possible round of showers \nnext Friday.",
